From af5240758d7fa1aacf065670d363df98da562ca8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oliver Hartkopp <socketcan@hartkopp.net>
Date: Fri, 13 Feb 2026 18:43:55 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 30/32] can: isotp: rework CAN frame structure access for CAN
 XL

As the layout of struct can[fd]_frame and struct canxl_frame differs all
functions that have been using a pointer to this CC/FD frame structure
have been changed in a way that they get a data pointer and a datalen.
Those parameters reference and describe the CAN frame data section.

Additionally to this change, the CAN frame head structures contain
different information which lead to new helper functions to fill and check
those CAN frame headers and to create and check the ISO PCI content.

No functional change for CAN CC/FD protocols.

Signed-off-by: Oliver Hartkopp <socketcan@hartkopp.net>
